tes": ["Incumbent Ben Ray Luján (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Ben Ray Luján seeks a second term against Republican Larry Marker, a little-funded challenger. New Mexico leans Democratic by about four points, and Luján enters with the advantages of incumbency, a dominant war chest, and no meaningful outside opposition spending. The Albuquerque Journal poll from late August showed him ahead 53 to 38, and markets on Kalshi, Polymarket, and PredictIt all price his win probability at 97 percent or higher.\n\nEvery major race rater, from Cook to Sabato to the Economist, places this in the Safe or Solid Democratic column. Marker has raised only about $33,000, leaving him unable to introduce himself to voters statewide. Barring an unforeseen shock, the race is expected to remain a low-drama incumbent win, with the main question being the size of Luján's margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.81}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9896, "margin": 15.5}]}